  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read http_profile.response_emission_binding and proxy.response_signing, the two units this root names directly (its dependency theorems THM-0062, 0063, 0065, 0022 and 0082 were re-read in this campaign or are unchanged in claim). In mcp-re-http-profile/src/sign.rs and sign/request.rs the request signers now take one RequestSignature (key id, created, expires, nonce) in place of four loose arguments, and compose_evidence_block was extracted; the response-emission files (custody/window_emission.rs, delegated_signer.rs, rejection/pre_052_direct_root.rs) are untouched. The proxy's response-signing sources (signing_window.rs and receipt/*) have no diff. Of the cited tests, eight changed bodies and I diffed each: the full_profile_test and sign.rs tests differ only by building the request signature as a RequestSignature with the same values; the two delegated_202 tests call a verify_default helper that runs verify_delegated_accepted_202 with the same verifier, the single accepted epoch, no revocation and the same instant; delegated_required_wiring_serves_verifies_and_rotates moved its loops into helpers (serve_and_verify_five, assert_replay_is_rejected_with_a_bound_receipt, delegated_signer_kid, assert_expired_key_fails_closed) that keep every assertion: five served and verified, delegated signer not the root, a 409 replay refusal still carrying a bound credential-chain receipt, a successor key with a different kid, and the unsigned 503 DelegatedSigningUnavailable past expiry. The claim, scope and premises are unchanged. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs. The mutation lane was not re-run by this reading; check-registries resolves every probe anchor.",
